# 16. FINANCIAL CALCULATION ENGINE

This section is extremely important.

All financial calculations must be performed through deterministic application logic, not by an AI model.

Implement a centralised financial calculation service.

CORE FORMULAS:

Net sales revenue = Sales excluding applicable taxes, after discounts and returns.

Cost of goods sold = Cost of inventory associated with products actually sold.

Gross profit = Net sales revenue - Cost of goods sold.

Gross margin percentage = Gross profit / Net sales revenue × 100.

Operating profit = Gross profit - Operating expenses.

Closing inventory quantity = Opening inventory + Stock received - Stock sold - Other stock-out movements + Restocked returns.

Inventory valuation = Quantity on hand × applicable inventory unit cost.

IMPORTANT ACCOUNTING REQUIREMENTS:

- Distinguish revenue from cash collected.
- Distinguish credit sales from paid sales.
- Distinguish purchases from cost of goods sold.
- Avoid counting supplier purchases and sold goods twice.
- Handle returns and discounts correctly.
- Handle tax separately.
- Maintain historical product cost snapshots.
- Support weighted-average inventory costing or another clearly configured valuation method.
- Show profit as an estimate where data is incomplete.

Do not call gross profit net profit.

Do not call operating profit final net income.

Add explanations beside financial metrics so non-accountants can understand them.

Use decimal-safe financial calculations and currency formatting.

